      "answer_text": "**Package:** `hermes-all-three`, in `hermes-plugins/`. It is one composed `ContextEngine` that applies A, B and D together through a single `select_context`, `get_tool_schemas` and `on_turn_complete`. You select it with `context.engine: all-three` in `config.yaml`. I did not read its engine code. I only saw its file list and its `pyproject.toml` dependencies on the three practice packages.\n\n**What stops three separate plugins from being active:** the Hermes plugin registry allows only one context engine.\n- `PluginRegistration.register_context_engine` (`hermes_cli/plugins.py:717`) refuses a second one. The code is `if self._manager._context_engine is not None: logger.warning(...); return`. It logs a warning and silently ignores the second registration.\n- This comes from `hermes-plugins/CONTRACT.md` (line 89 onward), which says \"all three\" must be one composed engine, not three co-active plugins.\n- The host also uses a single selected engine instance, `agent.context_compressor` (`agent/agent_init.py:2138`), and `context.engine` takes one name.\n\nThe `hermes-plugins/README.md` explains this under \"Why four packages — Hermes is single-select\". The LangGraph packages can stack three middlewares instead, because LangChain has no such limit."
    },
